@* Written in each component, not in an _Imports.razor, whose class Razor makes public (ADR-0201).
   Every product using is written with global::. The component lives in ExPivot.Components, where a
   plain "ExPivot.Engine" could be looked up against the ExPivot component class first, and a plain
   "ExGrid.X" against sibling types (the CS0426 trap in AGENTS.md). The Web namespace makes @on...
   handlers compile as event handlers rather than as plain HTML attributes. *@
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web
@using global::ExGrid
@using global::ExGrid.Cells
@using global::ExGrid.Chrome
@using global::ExGrid.Columns
@using global::ExGrid.Components
@using global::ExGrid.Rows
@using global::ExGrid.Selection
@using global::ExPivot.Chrome
@using global::ExPivot.Engine
@* Not the contract (ADR-0201): ExPivot places this frame around a menu or a panel in its own
   markup, and no Consumer places it. It is public only because Razor makes every component public,
   is hidden from a Consumer's editor, and may change in any version. *@
@attribute [System.ComponentModel.EditorBrowsable(System.ComponentModel.EditorBrowsableState.Never)]
@* ExPivot's frame around a menu or a panel (ADR-0061): where it stands and what closes it are
   ExPivot's; the content inside is the Chrome's. In the Field List it stands under its entry at the
   place the flow gives it, as wide as the pane and over what follows, so nothing needs a position
   ExPivot would have to measure; from the Pivot Toolbar it opens under the button that opened it,
   over the report — the Layout menu at the button's right edge. Escape closes it — unless a popup
   of the content's own is open, which ExPivot hears through the context and leaves the key
   to (ADR-0039). A menu's frame takes focus on a press on padding or a disabled command, without
   another Tab stop: Escape stays inside it (ADR-0061).

   In the pivot's Input Order (ADR-0240 section 6) the frame claims nothing (data-ex-claims=""), which
   makes it, holding the keyboard, the pivot's own: the grid may then hand the keyboard on from it. A
   key a control inside claims reaches the frame's handler in that key's turn, through the cascade
   (KeysName); one that bubbles up here from a draft's field, or is typed on the frame, goes after
   every input received so far. *@
<div class="@FrameClass" role="@Role" aria-label="@Label" @onkeydown="OnKeyDownAsync" data-ex-claims=""
     tabindex="@(Role == "menu" ? "-1" : null)" @onmousedown:stopPropagation @onfocusin:stopPropagation>
    <CascadingValue Name="@KeysName" Value="_keys" IsFixed="true">@ChildContent</CascadingValue>
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>The name the frame's key handler cascades under, to the ordered buttons inside it: a
    /// button that claims its keys hands the frame a key it does not answer itself in that key's turn.
    /// A button that cannot stop the key's propagation — a design system's — leaves the frame to hear
    /// it again after, which then finds nothing left to close.</summary>
    public const string KeysName = "ExPivotFrameKeys";

    private readonly Func<KeyboardEventArgs, Task> _keys;

    /// <summary>Creates the frame.</summary>
    public PivotPopupFrame() => _keys = OnKeyDownAsync;

    /// <summary><c>menu</c> for a menu, <c>dialog</c> for a panel.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string Role { get; set; } = "dialog";

    /// <summary>The frame's accessible name.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string Label { get; set; } = "";

    /// <summary>Whether it opens from the Pivot Toolbar, over the report.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Overlay { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Whether it stands at its button's right edge rather than its left.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool AlignEnd { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Escape was pressed inside it.</summary>
    [Parameter] public EventCallback OnEscape { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Every key heard inside it, in place of <see cref="OnEscape"/>.</summary>
    [Parameter] public EventCallback<KeyboardEventArgs> OnKey { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The Chrome's content.</summary>
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }

    private string FrameClass => (Overlay, AlignEnd) switch
    {
        (true, true) => "ex-pivot-popup ex-pivot-popup-overlay ex-pivot-popup-end",
        (true, false) => "ex-pivot-popup ex-pivot-popup-overlay",
        _ => "ex-pivot-popup",
    };

    private Task OnKeyDownAsync(KeyboardEventArgs e) =>
        OnKey.HasDelegate ? OnKey.InvokeAsync(e) : e.Key == "Escape" ? OnEscape.InvokeAsync() : Task.CompletedTask;
}
